-- title:
--   Fibrewise criterion for a zero scheme supported in U
-- statement:
--   Let $f\colon\mathcal C\to S$ be a proper flat morphism of schemes, let $U\subseteq\mathcal C$ be an open subscheme such that the composite $U\hookrightarrow\mathcal C\to S$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and let $g\colon T\to S$ be a morphism with $T$ locally Noetherian. Let $M$ be a module on $\mathcal C\times_S T$ which is invertible in the sense that every point has an open neighbourhood $V$ with the restriction of $M$ to $V$ isomorphic to the unit module, let $s\colon \mathbf 1\to M$ be a global section, and let $r$ be a natural number. Write $Z(s)$ for the zero-scheme ideal of $s$, i.e. the infimum of those ideal sheaf data $J$ on $\mathcal C\times_S T$ whose ideal on each affine open $V$ contains the ideal generated by the coefficients of $s$ on $V$. Assume that for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every $x\colon\operatorname{Spec} k\to T$ there is a relative effective Cartier divisor $D_x$ of degree $r$ for $f$ over $x\circ g$ — an ideal sheaf datum on $\mathcal C\times_S\operatorname{Spec} k$ whose closed immersion followed by the second projection is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation with fibre rank $r$ at every point — such that the ideal of $D_x$ is the pull-back of $Z(s)$ along the map $\mathcal C\times_S\operatorname{Spec} k\to\mathcal C\times_S T$ induced by $x$, and such that the support of that ideal lies in the preimage of $U$ under the first projection. Then there is a relative effective Cartier divisor $D$ of degree $r$ for $f$ over $g$ whose ideal is exactly $Z(s)$, whose support lies in the preimage of $U$, and which admits an isomorphism $e$ from $M$ to the line bundle $\mathcal O(D)$, the dual of the ideal module of $D$, carrying $s$ to the canonical section $1_D$ of that dual, i.e. $s$ followed by $e$ equals the `invModuleSection` of $D.I$.
--
--   This is the fibrewise criterion recognising the zero scheme of a section of an invertible module as a relative effective Cartier divisor of constant degree $r$, in the variant where smoothness of $f$ is weakened to flatness at the cost of requiring the fibrewise divisors to sit inside the smooth open $U$; the invertibility of $Z(s)$ is obtained from the fibrewise divisors via `isInvertible_I_of_supportedIn` and `isInvertible_zeroSchemeIdeal_and_flat`, and the trivialisation of $M$ as $\mathcal O(D)$ from `exists_iso_invModule_zeroSchemeIdeal`. It feeds the comparison between the relative Picard functor and divisors of degree $r$, being cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.exists_relEffCartierDiv_lineBundle_iso_of_forall_fibre_of_supportedIn`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.exists_relEffCartierDiv_lineBundle_iso_of_forall_fibre_of_supportedIn).
